From d8d145c52b78baaeda51cb95012509deddf7ff1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:24:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add episode-level raster donor test for LLM-grid policies

make_raster_donor_cache.py derives an LLM-Navigation cache under a new
model key in which every episode keeps its own metadata, status and
prediction files but its 37x100x100 grid is replaced: cross_scene (raster
of a random episode from another scene), within_scene (same scene,
different R2R trajectory_id so paraphrases are excluded) or block_permute
(own raster with the 10x10 token blocks permuted). Donors come only from
episodes whose source cache is complete; the assignment and a summary are
written next to the cache.

eval_raster_donor.sh evaluates a DAgger checkpoint (default: historical
LLM-Grid try5 iter28000) through the same SS-ETP-LLM option set as
eval_student_ablation.sh with the derived cache key, plus a control mode on
the unmodified cache, and prints the paired_analysis command.

Unlike zeroing the raster, a donor raster keeps the input in distribution,
so SR(control) - SR(cross_scene) measures episode-specific raster
information rather than the cost of an unseen all-zero map. block_permute
is a sanity check: the map encoder has no positional encoding and the
fusion is plain cross-attention, so the policy is invariant to it (checked
numerically on CPU: max output difference 2e-7 vs 0.19 for a 3-pixel shift).

No model, trainer or config code is touched.

